otenv", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Non-empty conf value > env var > ~~/.env dotenv (config.lua); .env is the canonical secret store, key-bearing confs are gitignored and keys must never be logged."}, {"id": "claude_lua_pattern_limits", "label": "Gotcha: Lua pattern limits (no {n,m}, no alternation)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lua patterns lack {n,m} quantifiers and | alternation; normalize() in anime_detect uses %d%d%d%d?p and per-token gsub loops with %f[] frontiers for that reason."}, {"id": "claude_zstd_convention", "label": "Convention: zstd at rest, resolve-on-read via hot dir", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Compress at rest (.zst), never store raw long-term; readers resolve logical names through a hot dir. The util/zstd.lua module is shared between ar_subs and autosubsync."}, {"id": "claude_cache_integrity", "label": "Convention: autosubsync transform-cache tied to retimed path", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Transform-cache entries carry the retimed file path, so wiping the ar_subs store self-invalidates them; both caches live under ~/.cache/mpv/ so a single wipe stays consistent."}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_playback_pipeline", "target": "claude_anime_detect", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_playback_pipeline", "target": "claude_ar_subs", "relation": "references"